course: dictionary
lesson: 10543
title: Light we cannot see
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: Sunlight contains many kinds of light, and some are too faint or too strange for our eyes to see. Ultraviolet light, or UV for short, is one of these hidden kinds. Its name is a clue: ultra means beyond, and violet is a colour we can see.
explain: UV light comes from the Sun, and it can harm us. «Skin also reacts to the world: ... burns if the sun's ultraviolet light is too strong.» So ultraviolet light is not just a fact to learn; it is a reason to wear sunscreen, a hat and sunglasses.
explain: Context gives you clues here. «Goldfish ... can see some ultraviolet light» and «we cannot» are set side by side, so the sentence tells you that ultraviolet is a light that some creatures can see and humans cannot.
fact: Ultraviolet light is a kind of light from the Sun that our eyes cannot see.
fact: UV is the short form of ultraviolet.
fact: Ultraviolet light can burn the skin and harm the eyes.
fact: «Jupiter has the most powerful auroras in the Solar System, glowing at its poles in ultraviolet light.»
fact: Some animals see what we cannot: «bees see ultraviolet patterns on flowers.»
exercise: «Skin ... burns if the sun's ultraviolet light is too strong.» What can too much ultraviolet light do? | Turn the sky green | *Burn the skin | Make you sleepy | Make your hair curl
exercise: What is ultraviolet light? | A kind of sound that bats hear | *A kind of light from the Sun that our eyes cannot see | A colour we see in rainbows | A type of sunscreen
exercise: «Scorpions glow blue-green under ultraviolet light.» What colour do scorpions glow under ultraviolet light? | Red | Yellow | White | *Blue-green
test: What is the short form of ultraviolet? | UK | UFO | UN | *UV
test: Which of these helps protect your skin and eyes from ultraviolet light? | *Sunglasses | A sunny day | Ice cream | A torch
exam: Why can bees see ultraviolet patterns on flowers when we cannot? | *Their eyes can detect ultraviolet light that ours cannot | Flowers only glow at night | They wear special glasses | Bees are much bigger than we are
